{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. \n*Early Life* is a section that describes his early life as a young count he was only a child when his father was murdered in 1152. \nHe was raised by King Baldwin III of Jerusalem who acted as his regent until he came of age. \n*Regency* is a section that describes the early years of his reign when the county was governed by King Baldwin III. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli became count in his own right in 1155 when he came of age. \n*Military Campaigns* is a section that describes his military campaigns against the Muslim forces of Nur ad-Din Zengi. \nHe fought alongside King Amalric of Jerusalem in several battles against the Muslims. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli played an important role in the Battle of Inab in 1149 where the Crusader forces were defeated. \nHe was captured by the Muslims and held prisoner for several years before being released. \n*Later Life* is a section that describes his later life as a count he became a wise and experienced leader. \nHe worked to strengthen the defenses of the county and to improve the economy. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli died in 1187 and was succeeded by his nephew Raymond IV Count of Tripoli. \n*Succession* is a section that describes the succession of the county after his death. \nThe county was passed down to his nephew who became the new count. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was an important figure in the history of the Crusades. \nHe played a significant role in the military campaigns against the Muslims. \n*Legacy* is a section that describes his legacy as a count he is remembered as a brave and wise leader. \nHe worked to strengthen the county and to improve the lives of his people. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was a notable figure in the history of th